--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY NOTES (web source is THE specification)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WidgetStatGrid.tsx is a PURE PRESENTATIONAL primitive: it receives already-resolved
`stats: StatGridItem[]` as a prop and has exactly TWO render branches —
  (1) stats.length === 0  → <EmptyState message="No stats available" />
  (2) otherwise           → a CSS grid of <StatCard> tiles.
There is NO data source / hook / loading / error / freshness in the source (the prompt's
data-source + i18n-key extraction both read "(none)"); those concerns are owned by the
data-bound widgets that COMPOSE this primitive (e.g. LifetimeStatsWidget). Reproducing
loading/error/stale/offline here would be invented scope the source does not have, so the
two real branches are reproduced faithfully and nothing more (Covenant #2).

Layout math ported VERBATIM from the source for cross-platform parity:
  • autoCols(count):  count % 3 == 0 → 3 ; else count % 4 == 0 → 4 ; else 2.
  • resolvedCols   :  compact ? 1 : (cols ?? autoCols(count)).
  • containerColsClass (container query on the WIDGET's own width, not the viewport):
        1 → always 1
        2 → always 2 (never collapses below 2)
        3 → @xs(<256px):1  @sm(256–384px):2  ≥384px:3
        4 → <384px:2  ≥384px:4
    Reproduced by StatGridLayout.effectiveColumns(target:bucket:) keyed off a width band
    measured from the grid via .onGeometryChange (iOS 18 / macOS 15 API).
  • gap            :  compact ? gap-2(8pt) : gap-3(12pt)  → TSSpacing.sm / .md.
Web `StatGridItem.value: string | number` → native stores the resolved display String, with
`int:`/`double:` convenience inits formatting through StatGridNumberFormat (grouped, en_US,
half-away-from-zero) so callers can pass a number exactly like the union. Web `valueColor`
(a Tailwind class) → a finite StatGridValueTone resolved to a P1/S9 token at the render
boundary. Trend shows only when BOTH trend && trendValue are present (web parity).

